==Analysis==
Incumbent president Ivo Josipović and opposition candidate Kolinda Grabar-Kitarović received the greatest number of votes in the first round. The result was notable for being much closer than expected in pre-election polls, with respective vote shares of 38.46% and 37.22%.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.jutarnji.hr/gdje-se-istopila-razlika--ankete-nisu-pogrijesile--rezultat-prvog-kruga-su-odlucila-tv-suceljavanja-/1264338/ | title = GDJE SE ISTOPILA RAZLIKA? 'Ankete nisu pogriješile, rezultat su odlučila TV sučeljavanja' | date = December 29, 2014 | work = [[Jutarnji list]] | language = hr | access-date = January 2, 2015 | archive-date = January 3, 2015 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20150103221002/http://www.jutarnji.hr/gdje-se-istopila-razlika--ankete-nisu-pogrijesile--rezultat-prvog-kruga-su-odlucila-tv-suceljavanja-/1264338/ | url-status = dead }}</ref> Political analyst [[Žarko Puhovski]] criticized the polls for having an inadequate sample and being overly reliant on telephone polling.<ref>{{cite web| url = http://www.vecernji.hr/predsjednicki-izbori2014/zasto-lazu-puhovski-ankete-se-rade-neozbiljno-i-zato-su-grijesile-981716| title = Zašto 'lažu'? Puhovski: Ankete se rade neozbiljno i zato su griješile | date = December 30, 2014 | work = [[Večernji list]] | language = hr}}</ref>

The new electoral law put into place by the [[Cabinet of Zoran Milanović|Milanović government]] had the effect of greatly reducing the number of polling stations in neighbouring Bosnia and Herzegovina for Croatian citizens residing there. This translated to a greatly reduced turnout there: from 50,859 in the first round of the 2009 presidential elections to 7,372 in 2014.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.izbori.hr/2009Predsjednik/rezultati/r_00_9901.html | title = POTPUNI SLUŽBENI REZULTATI IZBORA ZA PREDSJEDNIKA REPUBLIKE HRVATSKE | date = December 28, 2009 | work = Državno izborno povjerenstvo | language = hr | access-date = January 3, 2015 | archive-date = January 4, 2015 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20150104004202/http://www.izbori.hr/2009Predsjednik/rezultati/r_00_9901.html | url-status = dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.izbori.hr/106pre/rezult/1/rezultati.html?zup=22&gio=9901 | title = Privremeni službeni rezultati izbora za predsjednika Republike Hrvatske | date = December 30, 2014 | work = Državno izborno povjerenstvo | language = hr | access-date = January 3, 2015 | archive-date = January 4, 2015 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20150104004712/http://www.izbori.hr/106pre/rezult/1/rezultati.html?zup=22&gio=9901 | url-status = dead }}</ref> The Croatian Democratic Union agreed with its [[Croatian Democratic Union of Bosnia and Herzegovina|sister party in Bosnia and Herzegovina]] on organizing free buses for voters to polling stations for the second round.<ref>{{cite web| url = http://www.vecernji.hr/predsjednicki-izbori2014/hdz-organizira-besplatni-prijevoz-autobusima-na-biralista-u-bih-982750| title = HDZ organizira besplatni prijevoz autobusima na birališta u BiH | date = 6 January 2015 | work = [[Večernji list]] | language = hr}}</ref> Kolinda Grabar-Kitarović had received an overwhelming majority there in the first round. Josipović's campaign complained to the State Electoral Commission that offering free rides to polling stations constituted a donation which would violate electoral rules.<ref>{{cite web| url =http://www.novilist.hr/Vijesti/Hrvatska/Josipovicev-stozer-zatrazio-od-DIP-a-da-ispita-dopustenost-prijevoza-biraca-do-biralista-u-BiH| title = Josipovićev stožer zatražio od DIP-a da ispita dopuštenost prijevoza birača do birališta u BiH | date = 7 January 2015 | work = Novi List | language = hr}}</ref> However, votes of the diaspora still wouldn't change the outcome.<ref>{{cite news|last=Pavković |first=Jozo |title=Dijaspora prvi put na strani pobjednika, ali nije presudila rezultat izbora |url=http://www.vecernji.hr/predsjednicki-izbori2014/dijaspora-prvi-put-na-strani-pobjednika-ali-nije-presudila-rezultat-izbora-983633 |newspaper=Večernji list |date=12 January 2015 |access-date=12 January 2015 |language=hr}}</ref>

Around 60% of voters between ages 18 and 29 voted for Grabar-Kitarović, while Josipović was favoured by voters older than 60.<ref>{{cite news |last=Belak-Krile |first=Anita |title=NOVA GENERACIJA KONZERVATIVACA Oni ne pamte ni rat, ni SFRJ, slušaju narodnjake i izabrali su Kolindu |url=http://www.jutarnji.hr/oni-ne-pamte-ni-rat--ni-jugoslaviju--slusaju-narodnjake-i-aklamacijom-su-izabrali-kolindu/1274238/ |newspaper=Jutarnji list |date=14 January 2015 |access-date=15 January 2015 |language=hr |archive-date=15 January 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150115060525/http://www.jutarnji.hr/oni-ne-pamte-ni-rat--ni-jugoslaviju--slusaju-narodnjake-i-aklamacijom-su-izabrali-kolindu/1274238/ |url-status=dead }}</ref>

